WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.660
So my name is Cohl Furey and I'm a
postdoctoral fellow in theoretical

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.299
physics at Trinity Hall, University of
Cambridge.

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:18.060
So the short answer is that the octonions are this special number system in

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.650
pure mathematics and the opto neons
could be important for particle physics

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.430
because they seem to mirror the behavior
of certain elementary particles under

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:32.369
the strong and electroweak forces so the
real numbers are the numbers that you're

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.510
used to using in everyday life they span
from minus infinity to plus infinity and

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:42.059
they include numbers such as 0 1 2 3 4
and they also include other numbers like

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:47.400
irrational numbers like the number of pi
so we say that the real numbers are one

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.260
dimensional because we can lay out all
the real numbers on an infinitely long

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:58.140
line now the octo neons are not
one-dimensional it turns out that the OP

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.850
twenty ones are eight dimensional and
they also have some curious properties

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:07.229
so for example the real numbers are
commutative so that means that that a

00:01:07.229 --> 00:01:12.180
times B is always equal to B times a but
this isn't always true for the octo

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:19.009
neons also the real numbers are
associative and what that means is that

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:24.479
it's a a B and C like this where you
multiply the a and the B first is always

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:29.369
equal to a B C like this where you
multiply the B and C first but this

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:34.380
isn't true all the time in the octo
neons now it turns out that thanks to

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:39.569
these unusual properties of the octo
neons you can show that the octo neons

00:01:39.569 --> 00:01:43.200
are able to describe the behavior of
certain elementary particles under the

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.759
strong and electroweak forces

